   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi,\r<br>\r<br>Sorry, this is certainly quite a basic question, but what is the &quot;best&quot; \r<br>way (in terms of efficiency) to select the n first rows of each group \r<br>with dplyr ?\r<br>\r<br>Is there a special function, like n(), that would return the current row \r<br>number in the group and that could be used in a condition with\r<br>filter() ? Or am I just missing the obvious ?\r<br>\r<br>Thanks a lot,\r<br>-- Julien Barnier Centre Max Weber ENS de Lyon\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
