    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br>On Monday, March 3, 2014 7:18:09 AM UTC-8, Julien Barnier wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">Hi,\n<br>\n<br>Sorry, this is certainly quite a basic question, but what is the &quot;best&quot; \n<br>way (in terms of efficiency) to select the n first rows of each group \n<br>with dplyr ?\n<br>\n<br>Is there a special function, like n(), that would return the current row \n<br>number in the group and that could be used in a condition with\n<br>filter() ? Or am I just missing the obvious ?\n<br>\n<br>Thanks a lot,\n<br>-- Julien Barnier Centre Max Weber ENS de Lyon\n<br></blockquote></div></div></div>"
